    }
   },
   {
    "field": "special",
    "value": "no antibodies on its surface (a naive B cell carries surface antibody; the plasma cell does not)",
    "quote": "distinguishes a naïve B cell with antibody on its surface from an antibody-secreting plasma cell with no antibodies on its surface.",
    "source": {
     "section": "21.4 The Adaptive Immune Response: B-lymphocytes and Antibodies",
